      "level": 2,
      "content": "CONSTITUTIONAL DEVELOPMENT OF INDIA (1773–1947)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The constitutional timeline traces British legislative interventions in India from 1773 to 1947.",
        "Company Rule (1773–1858) was defined by early centralisation through Charter Acts of 1813, 1833, and 1853.",
        "Crown Rule began after 1857 via the Government of India Act, 1858, transferring power directly to the British Sovereign.",
        "Major political and communal reforms were introduced by the Indian Councils Act of 1909 (Morley–Minto Reforms).",
        "Structural legislative evolution culminated in the Government of India Act, 1935 and the Indian Independence Act, 1947."
      ],
      "id": "fzjfg77"
    },
