    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Regulating Act of 1773 was the first attempt by the British Parliament to regulate East India Company administration.",
        "Government of India Act, 1858 abolished the East India Company and transferred powers to the British Crown.",
        "Indian Councils Act, 1909 (Morley–Minto Reforms) introduced a separate electorate system for Muslims.",
        "Government of India Act, 1935 served as a primary structural source for the modern Constitution of India."
